# Gate submitters: one line per authorized key. <stable-id> <key type> <base64 key> [from-name].
# The optional from-name is a NAME, looked up on the host in /etc/pneuma-gate/from.conf ("name address" per
# line) and rendered as from="<address>" at install time. No host address is ever written in this repo.
# The key is DEDICATED to the gate: it is authorized here and nowhere else (not in root's authorized_keys).
# The private half lives only on the dev box at ~/.ssh/pneuma_gate_submit_ed25519; the lanes' gate client
# connects with it (ssh config: IdentityFile ~/.ssh/pneuma_gate_submit_ed25519, User pneuma-submit).
# The installer renders each line as a restrict + forced-command authorized_keys entry (root-owned file).
# The id is the identity the gate records and caps; a client cannot choose it.
